From fe46d6c9b1e345f8560cd7feeb806ad588bb23e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gex <gex@localhost>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 10:16:25 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland.drv: Have the compositor frame a window with a
 caption (xdg-decoration).

With zxdg_decoration_manager_v1, a top-level window with a caption asks
for server-side decoration, and Win32 leaves its caption and border to
the compositor (GetWindowStyleMasks): the surface is the window's
visible rect, inside them, and a configure's size is the client area's.
A compositor that places windows (gex_window_placement_v1) frames them
only when its host says it frames placed windows, WINEGEX_FRAMES=1 (gex's
HostWindows); such a window is placed but not unmanaged, and an origin
other than where Win32 put it is its frame having moved it: Win32 moves
it there. Windows without a caption, and every window when the
compositor says client_side or win32u's Decorated option is off, are
drawn by Win32 as before.
---
